1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,720
Graduation day is right around the corner.

2
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:07,240
Can you believe it?

3
00:00:12,860 --> 00:00:15,040
So, um, just wondering.

4
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:22,200
Why is your locker still so full?

5
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:23,640
Take your stuff home, girl.

6
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:28,080
Come on, I'll give you a hand.

7
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:29,380
Show me what you want to keep.

8
00:00:29,380 --> 00:00:30,020
Okay.

9
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:31,920
But you're definitely throwing out those papers.

10
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:32,500
Okay.

11
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:35,440
Too funny.

12
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:37,360
Is Hori your bestie or her mother?

13
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:41,380
Newsflash, you ain't packing so lightly yourself there.

14
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:42,160
Look who's talking.

15
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:44,360
You procrastinating pigs.

16
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:47,780
If you'd cleaned up a little every day, you'd be leaving like this.

17
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:49,920
Is that a free hand I see?

18
00:00:50,540 --> 00:00:51,860
Two, if I'm not mistaken.

19
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:52,660
In that case.

20
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:53,280
What?

21
00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:58,840
I swear, you guys.

22
00:00:58,840 --> 00:01:00,700
We're putting your muscles to good use.

23
00:01:00,820 --> 00:01:01,760
Holy crap, Hori.

24
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:04,200
You waited this late in the game to pack up shop?

25
00:01:04,220 --> 00:01:06,400
No, these jerks just dropped their junk on me.

26
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:07,380
Hold on.

27
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:09,640
Speaking of stuff, where are your bags?

28
00:01:10,020 --> 00:01:10,980
I planned ahead.

29
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:14,460
Put on my good boy pants and haul stuff back home every day.

30
00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:16,720
Please don't look at me like that.

31
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,360
Hey, I have that same CD.

32
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:20,120
Good taste.

33
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:22,240
Actually, I think this one is yours.

34
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:23,600
I just forgot to return it.

35
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:24,360
My bad.

36
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:25,280
It's all cool.

37
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:26,520
Better late than never, right?

38
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:28,180
If you say so.

39
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:31,040
Come to think of it, I have some DVDs I borrowed off you.

40
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:31,940
Huh?

41
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:33,740
And she's not the only one.

42
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:34,380
Huh?

43
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:36,900
There goes my easy commute home.

44
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:37,720
Farewell.

45
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:38,460
Zoe!

46
00:01:39,460 --> 00:01:39,940
Are you?

47
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:44,360
Wow, you lightened your load, but you still have so much.

48
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:47,740
It would make way more sense if a bigger, stronger dude carried it for you.

49
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,940
Like me or Ishikawa or...

50
00:01:49,940 --> 00:01:50,200
Hmm.

51
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:52,300
Ohori!

52
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:56,620
Oh, but why?

53
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:58,180
Oh, come on now.

54
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:00,000
It's not like he thinks of you as a dude.

55
00:02:00,220 --> 00:02:02,700
He meant that people can rely on you, which is a compliment.

56
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:03,140
Hmm.

57
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:03,240
Hmm.

58
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:03,740
Hmm.

59
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:03,840
Hmm.

60
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:52,280
Oh, come on now.

61
00:02:52,300 --> 00:03:22,280
Oh, come on now.

62
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:24,300
Remy.

63
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:40,480
Would you mind taking care of the tra...

64
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:40,880
Ugh.

65
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:42,760
Yet another distraction.

66
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:46,360
Is that a travel magazine?

67
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:47,660
Mm-hmm.

68
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:49,880
Oh, a zoo feature.

69
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:51,160
What do you think?

70
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:53,120
Want to visit a big herd of giraffes?

71
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:55,740
I mean, who wouldn't, but...

72
00:03:55,740 --> 00:03:57,540
Doesn't a day trip to the zoo sound fun?

73
00:03:57,780 --> 00:03:58,560
We should all go.

74
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:00,820
Is it the same one we went to before?

75
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:02,180
Not quite.

76
00:04:02,380 --> 00:04:03,160
Here, look.

77
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:04,420
Hmm.

78
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:06,800
That's a little more than a day trip.

79
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:08,280
I think it'd take at least two.

80
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:10,000
We'd also need a car.

81
00:04:10,180 --> 00:04:11,120
And money for a hotel.

82
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:14,140
If we get a car and a hotel room, you guys will go?

83
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:16,500
You're making her think this might happen.

84
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:19,020
Do not get Remy's hopes up higher than they already are.

85
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:20,180
Okay, Mom.

86
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:23,140
In all honesty, though, I would really like a car.

87
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:25,040
It would literally open up avenues.

88
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:27,260
I can't wait to get my license.

89
00:04:27,260 --> 00:04:32,520
If I had my own car, I could take you to way more places than just the zoo, you know?

90
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:33,660
We could go anywhere.

91
00:04:33,780 --> 00:04:33,940
Oh.

92
00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:34,960
Mm-hmm.

93
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:36,440
You sure could.

94
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:38,340
I, um...

95
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:42,040
I can't help but wonder if this actually goes beyond visiting a zoo.

96
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:43,180
I'm not sure I follow.

97
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:44,720
Okay, so Remy's kind of thirsty.

98
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:47,360
Hold your horses there.

99
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:50,220
You can leave as soon as you tell us what's bothering you.

100
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:51,760
I'm fine.

101
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:53,880
So we're gonna do this the hard way, then?

102
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:56,000
Sengoku, if you would be so kind.

103
00:04:56,140 --> 00:04:56,560
On it.

104
00:04:56,740 --> 00:04:58,700
I promise you, there's nothing wrong.

105
00:04:58,780 --> 00:05:00,040
I know you better than that.

106
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:01,820
Uh, Kono?

107
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:03,220
You have two choices.

108
00:05:03,580 --> 00:05:07,460
Let us help you or show Yanagi something I doubt he's seen but won't soon forget.

109
00:05:08,140 --> 00:05:09,260
Are you threatening her?

110
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:10,700
Remy's tough.

111
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:11,680
Do your worst.

112
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:12,780
Wait just a minute.

113
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:15,060
She's allowed to keep her thoughts to herself.

114
00:05:15,060 --> 00:05:18,880
You don't need to resort to violence or whatever it is you're...

115
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:19,460
Oh, wow.

116
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:20,360
Her cheeks?

117
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:25,120
There's no point to this since we can't understand her and you want her to talk.

118
00:05:25,540 --> 00:05:26,700
Sengoku, tell her.

119
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:28,380
It's a fairly rare face to see.

120
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:29,960
Take it all in while you can.

121
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:30,340
What?

122
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:33,380
Are you in any pain?

123
00:05:34,260 --> 00:05:34,600
No.

124
00:05:35,180 --> 00:05:36,360
It was like a massage.

125
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:37,920
It was?

126
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:40,300
So, here's the thing.

127
00:05:40,820 --> 00:05:42,400
It's really not that big of a deal.

128
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:49,140
Remy just thought it might be nice to go someplace fun with everybody while we're still in high school since we're nearly done.

129
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:52,600
But then you guys started talking about cars and licenses.

130
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:57,320
And I realized all those things have potential to take you far away from me.

131
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:58,440
And I don't want that.

132
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:02,480
They also have the potential to help with running everyday errands.

133
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:03,200
That's true.

134
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:06,920
Anyway, we can nix the zoo idea.

135
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:08,640
Remy was just tossing it out there.

136
00:06:08,680 --> 00:06:11,280
We don't need sporadic day trips to keep our friendship going.

137
00:06:11,660 --> 00:06:12,020
Really?

138
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:14,860
You won't treat me like a stranger the second you graduate?

139
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:16,520
Of course not.

140
00:06:16,900 --> 00:06:18,240
You aren't very easy to forget.

141
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:19,320
I know.

142
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:19,760
Huh?

143
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:23,980
As soon as I get my license, let's reconvene and plan a road trip.

144
00:06:24,380 --> 00:06:25,040
I'm game.

145
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:25,680
We're two.

146
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:27,360
Oh, how about a beach?

147
00:06:27,980 --> 00:06:29,660
Ah, you a fan of the sea breeze?

148
00:06:30,260 --> 00:06:31,600
Oh, Remy likes the beach.

149
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:32,660
Let's swim.

150
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:35,500
I only want to look at the water, not swimming it.

151
00:06:36,260 --> 00:06:38,280
Then after graduation, that's what we'll do.

152
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:43,760
We can make a pit stop at the zoo on the way there.

153
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:46,520
You could go all the time if you get a license as well.

154
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:48,020
But then who would ride shotgun?

155
00:06:48,260 --> 00:06:49,620
Oh, I want a shotgun.

156
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:50,920
Maybe take turns?

157
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:54,240
Hori?

158
00:06:55,860 --> 00:06:56,800
Earth to Hori.

159
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:02,020
She's down for the count.

160
00:07:03,180 --> 00:07:06,100
Carrying everyone's stuff must have really taken its toll on her.

161
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:09,520
Yes, ma'am.

162
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:10,560
I'm here.

163
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:20,340
I guess she just wanted a pillow.

164
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:24,540
She's frowning in her sleep.

165
00:07:26,140 --> 00:07:28,340
Well, that is one of her go-to faces.

166
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:32,300
Don't frown unless you actually want wrinkles on your forehead.

167
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:40,760
Eat, work, sleep.

168
00:07:41,060 --> 00:07:42,080
That's all you do, huh?

169
00:07:44,360 --> 00:07:45,520
You're so funny.

170
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:49,740
I hope days like these never end.

171
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:52,340
Even after high school.

172
00:07:52,340 --> 00:08:01,540
Looking back, if that one single incident hadn't happened.

173
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:08,340
I mean, well...

174
00:08:08,340 --> 00:08:11,840
If it hadn't happened.

175
00:08:13,460 --> 00:08:16,620
Lise give us till the last day of school to turn in our graduation essays.

176
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:18,820
I forgot about that.

177
00:08:18,820 --> 00:08:21,760
Speaking of graduation, I wonder what our picks look like.

178
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:23,460
Your guess is as good as mine, Hori.

179
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:26,300
All I remember was standing next to a guy I never even talked to.

180
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:26,700
Ishikawa!

181
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:27,640
You ready to bat?

182
00:08:27,820 --> 00:08:27,940
Yeah.

183
00:08:27,940 --> 00:08:29,380
And we still haven't spoken to this day.

184
00:08:29,520 --> 00:08:31,040
But you're in the same class.

185
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:33,520
Oh, sorry.

186
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:35,840
It's fine.

187
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:37,860
You girls up for some bad singing?

188
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:40,220
Did your sister pass that exam?

189
00:08:40,680 --> 00:08:41,720
Nah, she didn't.

190
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:43,640
Ugh, that majorly sucks.

191
00:08:44,420 --> 00:08:46,120
Oh, I'm glad I ran into you.

192
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:46,640
Why's that?

193
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:48,280
Just came from the council room.

194
00:08:48,540 --> 00:08:49,940
Ah, you finished cleaning?

195
00:08:50,260 --> 00:08:51,820
Yes, it's Spick and Span.

196
00:08:52,260 --> 00:08:52,860
Thanks, Gondo.

197
00:08:53,460 --> 00:08:53,760
Sakura!

198
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:55,480
I'm ready to go when you are!

199
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:57,200
Hey, perfect timing, Remy.

200
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:59,660
She looked so much better when she had longer hair.

201
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:02,740
She's so unfriendly.

202
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:05,020
Walk faster, geez!

203
00:09:05,020 --> 00:09:07,180
Get there when we get there, so stop rushing me.

204
00:09:07,180 --> 00:09:11,700
Oh, before I forget, so about that shop you mentioned the other day.

205
00:09:12,740 --> 00:09:13,640
Are you listening?

206
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:16,820
Do you know those boys?

207
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:17,600
Huh?

208
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:18,340
Oh.

209
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:19,680
No, I don't.

210
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:32,980
It's such a pain to take all my stuff home.

211
00:09:33,260 --> 00:09:35,900
Ugh, it's such a pain to take all my stuff home.

212
00:09:36,680 --> 00:09:38,260
I should have done it ages ago.

213
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,820
I should have done it ages ago, but I kept putting it off.

214
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:43,680
Attention students.

215
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:44,340
Attention students.

216
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:47,960
Please take the building at this time so the staff meeting may come up.

217
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:49,380
Yep, on my way.

218
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:57,620
Just one more week, and we'll be high school graduates.

219
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:03,160
I'm crossing my fingers that it gets a little warmer for graduation day.

220
00:10:03,180 --> 00:10:04,940
I'm crossing fingers and toes.

221
00:10:08,940 --> 00:10:09,340
OMG!

222
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:11,200
Did you see that guy?

223
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:13,020
He was like mega hot!

224
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:13,840
Wait, really?

225
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:14,700
He's a senior?

226
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:17,040
Oh, I wasn't paying attention.

227
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:21,620
Oh, wow.

228
00:10:21,940 --> 00:10:23,160
Surprised somebody's still here.

229
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:26,280
I think I left my phone inside my desk.

230
00:10:26,780 --> 00:10:28,500
And sure enough, there it is.

231
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:33,080
Hey.

232
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:34,760
This yours?

233
00:10:35,900 --> 00:10:36,420
Huh?

234
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:38,280
Is what mine?

235
00:10:38,660 --> 00:10:39,600
This silver thing.

236
00:10:39,920 --> 00:10:41,740
Pretty sure I saw you drop it just now.

237
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:43,060
It looks like an earring.

238
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:44,360
Um, bye.

239
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:46,260
Hey!

240
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:48,400
What the hell?

241
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:49,940
What a weirdo.

242
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:56,200
I'm not entirely sure why.

243
00:10:57,420 --> 00:11:00,940
But, ultimately, somehow.

244
00:11:00,940 --> 00:11:01,080
Somehow.

245
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:12,800
My high school days amounted to nothing.

246
00:11:13,880 --> 00:11:16,180
At least, that's how it feels.

247
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:18,500
People always wonder what if.

248
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:21,340
But dwelling on what could have been is pointless.

249
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:24,800
Although, you didn't have to wonder.

250
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:27,800
Mm-hmm.

251
00:11:34,100 --> 00:11:34,660
Miyamura?

252
00:11:39,220 --> 00:11:40,060
I'm sorry.

253
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:41,440
I was spacing out.

254
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:42,860
You okay?

255
00:11:43,420 --> 00:11:45,940
What's going on inside that adorable little head of yours?

256
00:11:46,700 --> 00:11:47,340
Hmm.

257
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:49,680
Just thinking.

258
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:53,140
There are so many different roads that led me to where I am today.

259
00:11:53,140 --> 00:11:55,500
I could have easily taken another route.

260
00:11:56,040 --> 00:11:57,260
And wound up somewhere else.

261
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:04,160
You know what?

262
00:12:04,580 --> 00:12:06,540
I think we're exactly where we're meant to be.

263
00:12:06,920 --> 00:12:09,300
We're together like this because that's how fate wanted it.

264
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:12,440
Maybe you're right.

265
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:17,840
There was a possibility of living in a world without you.

266
00:12:18,940 --> 00:12:20,860
But that world's not my reality.

267
00:12:22,040 --> 00:12:22,740
You're here.

268
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,160
Along with everyone else.

269
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:27,280
I'm not alone anymore.

270
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:29,120
Fate, he said.

271
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:33,580
I wonder if such a thing actually was responsible for bringing us together.

272
00:12:34,360 --> 00:12:36,380
Even if this fate doesn't really exist,

273
00:12:37,260 --> 00:12:39,760
I think the universe would have slowly, but surely,

274
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:42,220
moved me to the place I wanted to be.

275
00:12:42,220 --> 00:12:51,740
Next on the docket, we will have the farewell address from this year's valedictorian,

276
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:53,680
Kakaru Sengoku.

277
00:12:54,020 --> 00:12:54,720
Thank you, ma'am.

278
00:12:54,720 --> 00:13:19,240
Nice one, he's me.

279
00:13:19,240 --> 00:13:29,940
That big dummy!

280
00:13:29,940 --> 00:13:37,540
Spring is finally spring, and with it we have blossomed and come into our own as the 63rd class of Catecurity High School.

281
00:13:37,540 --> 00:13:41,680
All graduating students, please return to your-

282
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:42,440
Little punk!

283
00:13:42,660 --> 00:13:43,820
You ruined everything!

284
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:45,540
Sorry about that!

285
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:47,100
It was a complete accident, though!

286
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:48,360
Yo, Miyamura!

287
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:49,860
Nice sneeze, dude!

288
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:50,960
That wasn't nice!

289
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:53,300
There's your sense of humor, brud!

290
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:55,340
Excuse me, Ishikawa!

291
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:57,400
No, I lost him!

292
00:13:57,420 --> 00:13:58,040
Come on, man.

293
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:59,180
You're our valedictorian.

294
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:00,840
Should you really be tearing through the hallway?

295
00:14:01,460 --> 00:14:03,760
Though you sure tore it up with that hype speech!

296
00:14:04,780 --> 00:14:07,340
So, why were you chasing Miyamoto in the first place?

297
00:14:07,700 --> 00:14:09,820
Did you miss the beginning of my speech?

298
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:16,300
I've got to apologize to him later.

299
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:26,920
It's a beautiful day.

300
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:33,900
And I see you're enjoying it.

301
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:34,760
Mm-hmm.

302
00:14:35,420 --> 00:14:36,780
You chopped all your hair off.

303
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:38,900
Word spread about my piercings.

304
00:14:39,580 --> 00:14:40,240
And tats.

305
00:14:41,060 --> 00:14:42,100
I've got friends now.

306
00:14:42,900 --> 00:14:44,220
Plus, a really great girl.

307
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:52,260
I got used to you completely ignoring me, but today you finally looked.

308
00:14:55,020 --> 00:14:55,500
Yeah.

309
00:14:56,220 --> 00:14:57,220
And...

310
00:14:57,220 --> 00:14:59,140
I'll acknowledge you from now on.

311
00:15:04,140 --> 00:15:05,340
Guess this is goodbye.

312
00:15:10,860 --> 00:15:11,340
Congratulations.

313
00:15:11,980 --> 00:15:12,760
You made it through.

314
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:16,000
Ah, there you are.

315
00:15:16,300 --> 00:15:17,160
Come back down.

316
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:19,320
They want to get a group photo with everyone.

317
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:21,260
I know it's gorgeous out, but...

318
00:15:21,960 --> 00:15:22,260
Uh...

319
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:24,120
Is something wrong?

320
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:27,200
No.

321
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,680
The wind's pretty strong today.

322
00:15:34,400 --> 00:15:34,840
Teenagers.

323
00:15:35,300 --> 00:15:36,940
Not even half the class is here.

324
00:15:37,580 --> 00:15:39,600
Let's get a shot together while we wait!

325
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:40,660
Mind if I'm in it, too?

326
00:15:41,660 --> 00:15:42,920
Well, fine.

327
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,080
Now say cheese.

328
00:15:44,460 --> 00:15:46,140
Hey, the guys are graduating, too.

329
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:47,480
Take pictures of us, huh?

330
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:51,260
Why'd I devote any of my memory card to you fools?

331
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:54,100
Y'all wasted more than enough space in my brain as it is.

332
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:56,080
Come on, Yasuda!

333
00:15:56,220 --> 00:15:58,840
Some of us would like to document this pivotal moment in our lives!

334
00:15:59,340 --> 00:16:00,480
Party senpai!

335
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:03,700
I'm so sad I won't get to see you anymore!

336
00:16:04,700 --> 00:16:05,260
What's up?

337
00:16:05,700 --> 00:16:07,800
Well, you could always come over to my house.

338
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:10,300
Are you for real?

339
00:16:10,560 --> 00:16:11,300
Not too often, though.

340
00:16:12,100 --> 00:16:13,360
They're having one last hug.

341
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:15,120
Nice of you to indulge her for today.

342
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:21,200
It's the homestretch now.

343
00:16:26,600 --> 00:16:28,980
Um, have you seen Remy around recently?

344
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:31,160
Oh, yeah, I think she was...

345
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:32,280
Wait, that was someone else.

346
00:16:33,100 --> 00:16:33,360
Oh.

347
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:37,700
Hey, so...

348
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:40,560
I, uh...

349
00:16:40,560 --> 00:16:41,640
Well...

350
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:43,480
Sorry for the words, right?

351
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:49,120
Thank you.

352
00:16:51,180 --> 00:16:52,320
It's been a blast.

353
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:54,440
I really mean it.

354
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:56,880
My senior year was the highlight of my life,

355
00:16:57,040 --> 00:16:58,340
and part of that was because of you.

356
00:16:59,340 --> 00:17:01,860
I like both you and Yoshikawa so much.

357
00:17:02,060 --> 00:17:02,800
You're my friends.

358
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:04,880
And I'll never forget you.

359
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:07,220
Me, too.

360
00:17:08,100 --> 00:17:09,040
I won't forget.

361
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:10,340
I see.

362
00:17:10,860 --> 00:17:11,800
That's good to know.

363
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:13,660
Thanks again.

364
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:14,260
Anytime.

365
00:17:14,980 --> 00:17:15,820
And thank you.

366
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:16,540
Bye for now.

367
00:17:17,280 --> 00:17:17,820
Take care.

368
00:17:18,460 --> 00:17:19,240
See you around.

369
00:17:19,900 --> 00:17:20,760
Sure will.

370
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:20,840
Well...

371
00:17:20,840 --> 00:17:28,440
Guess it's best to leave all our high school baggage behind.

372
00:17:30,080 --> 00:17:30,680
Goodbye.

373
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:35,120
Oh, hi!

374
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:37,000
Congrats on a job well done!

375
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:39,660
You graduated, too, so congrats yourself!

376
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:41,480
I suppose I did, huh?

377
00:17:42,340 --> 00:17:43,160
Ah, that's right.

378
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:45,400
I have something extremely important to tell you.

379
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:46,460
Wow, this sounds major.

380
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:50,040
In the near future, I'd like to go somewhere with everyone.

381
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:51,520
As a group?

382
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:52,040
Right.

383
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:55,360
The other day, I got to talking with the student council crew,

384
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:56,620
and it made me realize something.

385
00:17:56,860 --> 00:18:00,180
Once I can legally drive, I'd like to take a trip with my friends.

386
00:18:01,260 --> 00:18:01,580
Friends.

387
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:03,380
The same as always.

388
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,020
Then there's Hori.

389
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:05,740
Kono sounded intrigued.

390
00:18:06,020 --> 00:18:06,360
Sure!

391
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:08,400
Sounds great, so count me in!

392
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:10,240
I certainly will.

393
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:11,020
Just wear your glasses.

394
00:18:11,760 --> 00:18:11,900
Huh?

395
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:15,320
It's unavoidable for some things to change once we graduate.

396
00:18:15,860 --> 00:18:19,380
But I know without a doubt the friends I have today will be the friends I have tomorrow.

397
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:20,540
Hey!

398
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:22,020
There's my special little boy!

399
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:23,580
Hello, Kyosuke.

400
00:18:24,140 --> 00:18:26,160
Whoa, is that Miyamura's dad?

401
00:18:26,260 --> 00:18:26,880
He's so young.

402
00:18:27,100 --> 00:18:28,300
I do see the resemblance.

403
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:29,780
What resemblance is that?

404
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:33,440
Come take a picture to preserve this lovely moment we're having, yeah?

405
00:18:33,460 --> 00:18:33,740
Okay.

406
00:18:34,300 --> 00:18:35,660
Let me go find one real quick.

407
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:41,000
Why in the hell would you go someplace you're not even welcome, you poor excuse for a father?

408
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,300
I thought it would be a good chance to have some time fun.

409
00:18:43,300 --> 00:18:43,540
Damn it!

410
00:18:43,660 --> 00:18:45,940
What kind of grown-ass man can't pull off a student's high?

411
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:50,340
Surely you'd like to meet up with your own parents, right, Miyamura?

412
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:52,220
My folks stopped by for a bit.

413
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:53,660
They had to hurry and get back to work.

414
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:55,840
Aw, don't get mad, honey bun.

415
00:18:56,280 --> 00:18:57,320
You want me to be happy?

416
00:18:57,420 --> 00:18:58,800
Then shut up and get lost!

417
00:18:59,780 --> 00:19:01,500
Okay, I'm calling for a truce.

418
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:04,680
There, got it.

419
00:19:04,980 --> 00:19:06,400
Yura, you're too much.

420
00:19:06,560 --> 00:19:07,960
I think that I'm seriously...

421
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:08,100
Just too.

422
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:10,640
Moto, what a surprise.

423
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:11,380
Hi.

424
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:13,240
I take it this is your little sister?

425
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:14,380
That's right.

426
00:19:14,920 --> 00:19:16,520
You come all this way to pick up your brother?

427
00:19:16,920 --> 00:19:20,140
I'm here because Mom wanted me to let you know you have to come home early today.

428
00:19:20,640 --> 00:19:22,960
Plus, I figured I could see what my new school would be like.

429
00:19:23,580 --> 00:19:24,280
Oh wow!

430
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:25,220
You don't stay!

431
00:19:25,520 --> 00:19:28,240
If that ceremony wasn't so darn long, I'd be home now!

432
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:31,380
But no time like the present, so let's get our butts and gear and book it, sis!

433
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,400
Guess I'll see you when I see you!

434
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:33,880
Okay, bye!

435
00:19:34,060 --> 00:19:34,240
Bye!

436
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:34,480
Bye!

437
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:37,880
You didn't lose any pep through all three years.

438
00:19:37,940 --> 00:19:39,280
The song was right with the world.

439
00:19:43,740 --> 00:19:44,800
Question for you.

440
00:19:44,880 --> 00:19:45,860
Go ahead and ask me.

441
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,560
You're really my brother, right?

442
00:19:48,940 --> 00:19:49,820
Better believe it.

443
00:19:49,820 --> 00:19:56,360
Miyamura!

444
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:56,480
Miyamura!

445
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:59,040
We're getting sushi to celebrate!

446
00:19:59,160 --> 00:19:59,700
You wanna come?

447
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:01,740
Oh yeah!

448
00:20:02,240 --> 00:20:02,560
Sweet!

449
00:20:02,820 --> 00:20:03,680
Let's get going then!

450
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:05,940
Kyosuke's gonna be so excited to see you there.

451
00:20:06,160 --> 00:20:07,040
Maybe too excited.

452
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:08,080
To the sushi!

453
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:10,640
There's no distance.

454
00:20:11,760 --> 00:20:13,880
I've never been this close to someone before.

455
00:20:14,860 --> 00:20:15,600
In my life.

456
00:20:17,660 --> 00:20:19,140
Boundaries don't apply to us.

457
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:21,660
And I used to be terrified of that.

458
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:24,740
It shook me to my core, Hori.

459
00:20:25,740 --> 00:20:27,840
But you know, because of you,

460
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:32,900
I felt a whirlwind of emotions I wasn't even aware I could feel.

461
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:38,840
I don't think either of us realized how nerve-wracking

462
00:20:38,840 --> 00:20:41,200
simply being yourself around other people could be.

463
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:42,840
No fronts.

464
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:44,380
Just us.

465
00:20:45,420 --> 00:20:47,160
Gradually breaking down our walls.

466
00:20:48,280 --> 00:20:51,140
But you made me realize that and then some.

467
00:20:52,020 --> 00:20:53,600
And I find myself asking,

468
00:20:54,460 --> 00:20:55,640
what can I do for you?

469
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:58,500
How many ways can I make you smile?

470
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:01,340
You're one of the strongest people I know.

471
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:03,800
Yet still so fragile.

472
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:05,980
So delicate.

473
00:21:07,280 --> 00:21:08,260
So precious.

474
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:13,100
Instead of a shadow,

475
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:16,440
bright sunny days are what follow behind you.

476
00:21:17,820 --> 00:21:18,920
My whole life,

477
00:21:19,420 --> 00:21:20,900
the only person I knew this well

478
00:21:20,900 --> 00:21:22,080
was myself.

479
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:27,960
I was oblivious to how breathtaking the world could truly be.

480
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:31,780
And you came in and shattered my reality.

481
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:33,600
Thank you.

482
00:21:34,860 --> 00:21:37,200
You told me you wanted a future with me.

483
00:21:38,340 --> 00:21:38,960
Thank you.

484
00:21:42,300 --> 00:21:43,920
But what can I do for you?

485
00:21:45,500 --> 00:21:47,520
How can I repay you for what you've done?

486
00:21:47,520 --> 00:21:51,500
Hurry up!

487
00:21:52,180 --> 00:21:52,880
Mia Moura!

488
00:21:59,380 --> 00:21:59,900
Wow.

489
00:22:00,900 --> 00:22:03,400
The spring sky is bluer than I've ever seen.

490
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:07,240
If I could give you this very sky as a gift,

491
00:22:07,860 --> 00:22:08,860
I would in a heartbeat.

492
00:22:09,760 --> 00:22:10,320
And again.

493
00:22:12,020 --> 00:22:12,360
Nah.

494
00:22:13,180 --> 00:22:14,240
I know what you'd like.

495
00:22:15,280 --> 00:22:17,520
A cake with tons of whipped cream on top.

496
00:22:18,580 --> 00:22:19,700
That's more your style.

497
00:22:19,700 --> 00:22:22,480
Bye.

498
00:22:24,440 --> 00:22:25,480
Bye.

499
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:28,260
Bye.

500
00:22:30,460 --> 00:22:32,740
Bye.

501
00:22:42,860 --> 00:22:43,300
Bye.

502
00:22:43,300 --> 00:23:13,280
Thank you.

503
00:23:13,300 --> 00:23:43,280
Thank you.

504
00:23:43,300 --> 00:24:13,280
Thank you.

